---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Tools" description="The 10 MCP tools the uap-analyzer server exposes: list_corpus, analyze_video, extract_frame, describe_image, analyze_pdf, search_corpus, index_corpus, flir_hud_ocr, transcribe_audio, detect_objects.">

  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">

    <section class="mb-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
        <span class="stamp text-accent-green">// TOOL REFERENCE · v0.4.3</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4 leading-tight text-text">MCP tools</h1>
      <p class="text-base text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl prose-body">
        Ten tools the LLM session can call by name. All return text or structured JSON; raw media stays in the container. Original Phase 3 backlog (audio, HUD-OCR, object detection) shipped across the v0.2.x – v0.4.x releases. v0.4.1 + v0.4.2 closed 22 hardening findings surfaced by two rounds of tribunal review — see <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">.tribunal/reports/</code> in the repo for the audit trail. v0.4.3 flipped the default vision model to <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">qwen2.5vl:7b</code> after a Release_2 frame where the prior default fabricated a confident negative on a redacted IR target lock — see <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">reports/dod_111720765_target_lock.md</code>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-4 font-mono">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text">/// LIVE — 10 OPERATIONAL</h2>
        <span class="text-[10px] text-accent-green tracking-widest flex items-center gap-2 hidden sm:inline-flex">
          <span class="inline-block w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-accent-green shadow-green-glow pulse-soft"></span>
          v0.4.3 · 2026-05-24
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-5">

        <div class="bg-panel rounded-sm p-5 border border-border hover:border-accent-green/60 transition">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono text-accent-green mb-2 tracking-widest">[ T-01 ] CORPUS</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent mb-2 font-mono"><code class="bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-base">list_corpus</code></h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mb-2 prose-body">
            List indexed files. <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">kind='video' | 'pdf' | 'image' | None</code>; <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">filter</code> substring match against the relative path; <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">rescan=True</code> walks <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">UAP_DATA_DIR</code> and refreshes the index first.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed prose-body">
            Returns a flat array of <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">&#123;path, kind, size_bytes, duration_s, width, height, page_count&#125;</code> plus aggregate <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">count</code> and <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">fts_indexed</code> counters.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-panel rounded-sm p-5 border border-border hover:border-accent-green/60 transition">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono text-accent-green mb-2 tracking-widest">[ T-02 ] VIDEO</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent mb-2 font-mono"><code class="bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-base">analyze_video</code></h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mb-2 prose-body">
            <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">mode='metadata'</code> runs <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">ffprobe</code> and returns codec, bitrate, fps, duration, dimensions. <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">mode='frames'</code> samples N frames at evenly-spaced timestamps and caches them. <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">mode='describe'</code> additionally vision-describes each sampled frame via ollama.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed prose-body">
            Default sampling: 4 frames at 25/50/75/100% of duration. FLIR-aware prompting suppresses the model's tendency to hallucinate HUD elements from training-data UAP footage.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-panel rounded-sm p-5 border border-border hover:border-accent-green/60 transition">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono text-accent-green mb-2 tracking-widest">[ T-03 ] VIDEO</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent mb-2 font-mono"><code class="bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-base">extract_frame</code></h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mb-2 prose-body">
            Pull a single frame at a given <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">timestamp</code> (seconds). <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">width</code> rescales; <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">return_base64=True</code> embeds the JPG in the tool response (use for frames the LLM should see).
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed prose-body">
            Cached. Re-requesting the same frame is fast. The cache lives under <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">UAP_CACHE_DIR/frames/</code>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-panel rounded-sm p-5 border border-border hover:border-accent-green/60 transition">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono text-accent-green mb-2 tracking-widest">[ T-04 ] IMAGE</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent mb-2 font-mono"><code class="bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-base">describe_image</code></h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mb-2 prose-body">
            Vision-describe any photo or extracted frame. FLIR-format input gets a thermal-anchored prompt (grayscale, redaction-disclaimer, 3-5 sentence constraint). Non-FLIR uses a generic prompt; pass your own via <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">prompt</code>.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed prose-body">
            Backed by <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">llama3.2-vision:11b</code> on a local ollama instance. ~10 s per frame. <em class="text-warm not-italic">Caveat:</em> the model is unreliable on this corpus — see the <a href="/findings" class="text-accent no-underline hover:underline">findings</a> for documented hallucinations.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-panel rounded-sm p-5 border border-border hover:border-accent-green/60 transition">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono text-accent-green mb-2 tracking-widest">[ T-05 ] PDF</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent mb-2 font-mono"><code class="bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-base">analyze_pdf</code></h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mb-2 prose-body">
            <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">mode='metadata'</code> returns pypdf metadata + page count. <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">mode='text'</code> pulls text via pdfplumber. <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">mode='ocr'</code> rasterizes pages at 200 dpi and OCRs via Tesseract. <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">mode='summary'</code> chains text/OCR → qwq:32b summarizer.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed prose-body">
            Whenever extracted text exceeds 200 chars, the result is auto-upserted into the FTS5 index — every successful analyze becomes searchable.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-panel rounded-sm p-5 border border-border hover:border-accent-green/60 transition">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono text-accent-green mb-2 tracking-widest">[ T-06 ] SEARCH</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent mb-2 font-mono"><code class="bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-base">search_corpus</code></h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mb-2 prose-body">
            SQLite FTS5 bm25 search across every indexed PDF. Returns a ranked list with <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">«match»</code>-highlighted snippets. <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">k</code> controls the result count; <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">kind='pdf'</code> currently the only indexed kind.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed prose-body">
            FTS5 syntax operators apply — <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">range AND fouler</code>, <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">"Persian Gulf"</code>, <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">strait*</code>, <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">NEAR(orb fly, 10)</code>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-panel rounded-sm p-5 border border-border hover:border-accent-green/60 transition">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono text-accent-green mb-2 tracking-widest">[ T-07 ] PIPELINE</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent mb-2 font-mono"><code class="bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-base">index_corpus</code></h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mb-2 prose-body">
            Bulk text + OCR-fallback + FTS-index pipeline across every PDF in the corpus. <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">force=True</code> re-extracts even when cached; <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">ocr_fallback=False</code> skips Tesseract for text-only runs.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed prose-body">
            Expect 5–15 minutes wall-clock for a fresh tranche (Tesseract is the bottleneck). Cached results are reused on subsequent runs — call this once after a new release lands.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-panel rounded-sm p-5 border border-border hover:border-accent-green/60 transition">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono text-warm mb-2 tracking-widest">[ T-08 ] FLIR · v0.2.0 / v0.2.1</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent mb-2 font-mono"><code class="bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-base">flir_hud_ocr</code></h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mb-2 prose-body">
            Extract burned-in FLIR HUD overlay fields — classification stamp, mode (BLK/WHT/IR/TV/CAM/NUC), zoom (x4.0 or NAR/MED/WIDE), range_nm, bearing_deg, elevation_deg, timecode — from sampled frames. Two extraction modes:
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mb-2 prose-body">
            <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">mode='ocr'</code> (default) — tesseract on per-corner crops with light preprocessing, then regex-parse. Fast and cheap. Best for clear, high-contrast overlays.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed prose-body">
            <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">mode='vision'</code> — qwen2.5vl:7b via ollama with structured-JSON output. Slower (~1.5s/frame after model load) but accurate on FLIR HUDs where tesseract struggles. Smoke results: 5/5 candidate clips surfaced stable readings vs 1/5 in ocr mode.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-panel rounded-sm p-5 border border-border hover:border-accent-green/60 transition">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono text-warm mb-2 tracking-widest">[ T-09 ] AUDIO · v0.3.0</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent mb-2 font-mono"><code class="bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-base">transcribe_audio</code></h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mb-2 prose-body">
            Speech-to-text via faster-whisper (CPU, int8). Extracts audio from video/audio files through ffmpeg (16 kHz mono WAV in cache), runs the model, returns timestamped segments + full text + auto-detected language. Default model <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">base.en</code> (75MB, ~4× realtime on CPU); bump to <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">small.en</code>/<code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">medium.en</code> for jargon-heavy clips.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed prose-body">
            Module-level model cache; audio extract result is cached on disk; whisper inference result lands in the SQLite cache. <em class="text-warm not-italic">Corpus note:</em> current UAP videos all have audio streams but no audio content — declassified footage has the cockpit audio stripped. Tool is verified end-to-end and ready for any future audio-bearing material.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-panel rounded-sm p-5 border border-border hover:border-accent-green/60 transition">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono text-warm mb-2 tracking-widest">[ T-10 ] DETECT · v0.4.0</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent mb-2 font-mono"><code class="bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-base">detect_objects</code></h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mb-2 prose-body">
            YOLOv8/v11 object detection (ultralytics, CPU-only torch). Samples N frames (or one timestamp/single image), returns per-timestamp <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">[label, confidence, bbox]</code> lists plus a cross-frame aggregation (total + by-label counts + top-5 ranked labels). Default <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">yolov8n</code> (~6MB, ~150-300ms/frame); <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">classes=['airplane', 'person']</code> filters to COCO whitelist.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed prose-body">
            <em class="text-warm not-italic">FLIR caveat:</em> COCO has 80 ordinary-world classes — no category for thermal blobs. Smoke shows every IR contact gets nearest-neighbor-labeled as <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">kite</code> at 0.27-0.58 confidence. Useful diagnostically: clusters of low-conf <code class="text-xs bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">kite</code> at consistent bboxes across frames is a signature of a tracked unmoving thermal contact.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-4 font-mono">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text">/// PLANNED</h2>
        <span class="text-[10px] text-muted tracking-widest hidden sm:inline">CORPUS-AWARE</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-3xl prose-body mb-4">
        With all four primitives shipped (HUD-OCR, audio, detection, vision-describe), the next wave is composition. Each draws on the existing tools rather than adding new inference.
      </p>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-panel/60 rounded-sm p-5 border border-border/60">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono text-muted mb-2 tracking-widest">// CONCEPT</p>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-text mb-2 font-mono"><code class="text-sm bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">cross_corpus_thread</code></h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed prose-body">Given a search query, return PDF hits + matching video timestamps (where vision-describe mentions the same entity). Knits the FTS5 index to the video-describe results.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-panel/60 rounded-sm p-5 border border-border/60">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono text-muted mb-2 tracking-widest">// CONCEPT</p>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-text mb-2 font-mono"><code class="text-sm bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">generate_report</code></h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed prose-body">Take a topic + corpus query, return a markdown report with citations. Synthesizes the manual reports/ pattern already in the repo.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-panel/60 rounded-sm p-5 border border-border/60">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono text-muted mb-2 tracking-widest">// CONCEPT</p>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-text mb-2 font-mono"><code class="text-sm bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">compare_videos</code></h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed prose-body">Two video paths in, structural diff out — same sensor / different sensor, same mode / mode-flip, HUD overlap, vision-describe semantic overlap.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-panel/60 rounded-sm p-5 border border-border/60">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono text-muted mb-2 tracking-widest">// CONCEPT</p>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-text mb-2 font-mono"><code class="text-sm bg-code-bg border border-code-border px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-accent">compare_to_known</code></h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed prose-body">Match candidate frames against a library of known mundane explanations (balloons, satellites, ATFLIR artifacts). Reference library still to build.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>

</Base>
